  "name": "Circle of the Wurm",
  "type": "subclass",
  "img": "modules/grimnir-lyonesse/assets/icons/faithtoken-dragon-head.svg",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>Deep within the wind-scoured moor called the Promise, where standing stones lean and black tarns mirror the sky, dwell the Druids of the Circle of the Wurm. These pools and circles are thresholds to the Otherworld, and here the Druids keep watch, walking paths shared with both the Fey and the black dragons that haunt the marsh. Their bond with those dragons is ancient and unsettling. When a clutch yields a flawed egg, it is not destroyed but entrusted to the Circle. Through a secret rite, a chosen Druid receives the hatchling’s spirit at the moment of its birth. The union is never perfect. The dragon’s flaws mark the Druid’s body, twisting spine or limb, while its instincts coil within their mind. It is restless, hungry, and half-remembering a life never lived. Some claim the ritual was gifted by the Fey, stolen from a distant land. Whatever its origin, those who bear the spirit of a wurm are creatures of awe and dread.</p>"
    },
    "source": {
      "custom": "Legends of the Round Table: Chivalric Handbook",
      "page": "46",
      "rules": "2024"
    },
